# JDK 21 (Temurin 21.0.13+9, Ubuntu 26.04.1, linux/amd64). A full JDK, not a JRE:
# Ghidra compiles Java GhidraScripts (REA's bridge and our ghidra_scripts) at run
# time with the in-process javax.tools compiler, which a JRE lacks.
JDK_IMAGE=eclipse-temurin:21-jdk@sha256:ebfbb18d11ff163ee83b21258acf12248af48d22a0fdfdc68fa1a1516c05976a

# upx-ucl from the base image's Ubuntu archive (the sweep upx -d-s UPX-marked samples).
UPX_VERSION=4.2.4-1.1build1

# Installer unwrapping (installer.py). The base image's archive is Ubuntu 26.04 "resolute"
# (not noble): versions read with `apt-cache policy` inside JDK_IMAGE on 2026-11-09.
# 7-Zip's NSIS handler extracts files only (no [NSIS].nsi since 15.05); the sweep decodes the
# script's string table itself. innoextract 1.9 (the latest release) reads Inno Setup up to
# 6.0.5; newer installers are attempted and fail as a warning.
SEVENZIP_VERSION=26.00+dfsg-1
INNOEXTRACT_VERSION=1.9-3
# Fixture regeneration only (rea-fixtures stage builds deploy/rea/fixtures/installer.exe).
NSIS_VERSION=3.10-2ubuntu2

# capa 10.0.0 (flare-capa wheel + deps, hash-locked in capa-requirements.txt), with the
# same release's rules (capa-rules tag) and FLIRT signatures (capa tag, sigs/ only).
